[Music]  what is up everybody its Anna Mack here  for anime uproar and we have finally  received official news about the Code  Geass sequel fukkatsu no Arusha or  Lelouch of the resurrection including  the release date but as excited as you  might be after over a year and a half of  waiting for any real news about the  sequel trigger warning it's not all good  news as the official Code Geass website  and various other news outlets are  reporting the sequel will not be a full  third season but rather just a single  movie that will be released in February  of 2019 when the sequel was first  announced back in November of 2016 it  was presented as a third chapter in the  story so knowing that Code Geass had two  seasons which were the first two  chapters most assumed that this new  third chapter would be a full third  season however it turns out that even  though the sequel will be officially  released more than two years after it  was first announced meaning that there  was plenty of time to create an entire  new season all we are getting is a movie  but it's not all bad news because this  movie will indeed include brand-new  material and a continuation to the Code  Geass stories so fans are getting new  official content and if this movie does  extremely well who knows maybe a new  season will be greenlit once they  realize that there is a lot of money to  be made similar things have happened in  the past in addition to the first PV  that was released over a year ago we  just received a new short teaser for the  sequel a teaser which features some  captivating shots of landscapes it's  Australia we all know it and we also see  a brief glimpse of c2 along with what  appears to be a brand new character if  you've been following our videos here on  the channel and also our discussions on  our discord server you know that for a  long time we believe that the plot of  the sequel will revolve around  discovering more about the true origins  of Geass power my good friend soul maka  in particular has been saying for a long  time that the brief scenes we see of  Kornelia visiting ancient temples in the  original pv for the sequel  evidence that she has been trying to  research Geass in order to clear her  sister Euphemia's name after what  happened in the original series and we  all know that the world of Code Geass is  fascinating and there is a lot more  going on there than might appear at  first glance as I already talked about  in many of our Code Geass videos for  example I believe that the thought  elevators and the collective unconscious  from the original series were created by  an ancient civilization known as the  Ragnar s and the power of Geass  originated with this ancient  civilization this new character that we  see in the teaser definitely looks a lot  different than the rest of the  characters in the series and we even see  some lines on the characters face that  look a lot like the lines on the faces  of the ancient Geass users that we see  in the Geass sequences or flashbacks  however you want to call them so my  guess is that the new plot will be  centered around discovering the origins  of Geass and the ancient civilization  known as the Ragnar s who first  constructed the thought elevators this  new character might be a descendant of  this ancient civilization and he or she  might be trying to protect the secret of  Geass from being discovered since I  personally loved the interesting world  that Code Geass establishes I am  definitely excited about the prospect of  learning more about Geass power and its  origins and since I always believed that  Lelouch survived being stabbed by Suzaku  at the end because he had obtained code  from Charles and became immortal and I  even made videos on this I could easily  get on board with this sequel even  though obviously I wish we were talking  about a full-season rather than a movie  because it is extremely difficult to  follow up on a 50 episode iconic anime  with a brief movie sequel however as I  said if the movie is successful who  knows what could happen my big problem  and yes there is a problem is this the  three recap movies that came out in the  past year were not just recap movies I  wish they were but they weren't usually  I don't pay attention to recap films at  all because I feel such films may be  good in terms of getting someone who  hasn't seen the anime interested in  watching it but after watching the anime  seeing a movie trying to condense the  story you love is just torture in my  opinion anyway I don't know how you guys  feel  but with these Code Geass films there  have been some major changes to the  story and I don't mean just cutting out  to the story because of time constraints  I mean things like changing the fact  that Shirley shot Valletta in the  original series in order to protect  Lelouch to diit hard shooting her  instead of Shirley this is a ridiculous  change in my opinion because while I  love both Valletta and Shirley shooting  Valletta was a crucial moment of  character development for Shirley she is  a kind and innocent person a person who  doesn't want to harm anyone but her love  for Lelouch leads her to do things that  she could never have done otherwise and  that is such an important aspect of her  character but if changing that wasn't  enough Shirley doesn't die in the recap  movies she is still alive and present as  Emperor Lelouch is stabbed by Suzaku in  the z-row costume at the end of the  story like what this means that the  creators of Code Geass have established  an alternate timeline with the film's a  timeline that doesn't match up with the  original story if you want to know more  about the changes in the recap films I  will link to a fox and anime video in  the description he did a good job of  going over everything so there's no  point of me repeating it here but  needless to say these changes have  really upset me not because I want  Shirley to be dead I loved her as a  character and her death was for me the  single most heartbreaking moment in the  entire story I am upset because I  considered the creation of an alternate  timeline to be a total cop-out it means  that fukkatsu no Dhanush will not be a  true sequel to the original story we  love instead it will be an alternate  what-if scenario that we can easily just  ignore now I can understand how a show  like steins gate that is based around  time-travel and alternate timelines can  make a sequel like steins gate 0 but to  do that to a completely differential  like Code Geass feels wrong to me it's  basically saying hey if you like the  sequel great but if you don't then just  pretend like it never happened and  that's not how a writer should ever  approach their own story and I know what  you're thinking but bro you would so  hype why are you no longer hype well  random person from Denmark I will still  give the sequel a chance and if it is  popular I hope that an entire series  will come out of this but if we do get a  series I wanted to follow the original  not be some alternate timeline if as a  writer and a creator you have the  courage to create a sequel to an already  beloved in establish  to work then you should have the courage  to make it a true sequel and not a  what-if scenario but that is my opinion  let me know what you guys think are you  still excited for the Code Geass sequel  or has the alter and timeline stuff  soured it for you a bit let me know down  in the comments you don't have to agree  with me I completely respect different  opinions if you want to discuss the  sequel feel free to join our discord  server link in the description the  entire server is set up as a tribute to  Code Geass and there are many hardcore  fans in there that you can talk to just  stay up to date on all the latest Code  Geass info be sure to subscribe to this  channel and hit that notification bell  as always thank you all so much for  watching and until next time see us  space cowboys  [Music]

